A||||12||dodger||Spun||||4||
Z||000000||dodger||06-10-2000||09:30 PM||||Whew...a close one!<BR>So I was on the way to work yesterday morning, stopped at a stop sign waiting to turn left onto a 45mph two lane road, busy with trucks and commuters. Then a small opening appeared in front of a big-rig, and I hit it. Only problem was, I was on a slight uphill incline and I spun-out and started left. This meant I did not have the speed to beat the truck. So I hit it harder and spun into the opposing lane and onto the shoulder, ahead of the on-coming cars, facing the wrong direction. So I backed up going the wrong direction onto the road I just came out of, turned around and started over. Gotta watch those quick moves!||||reg||4
Z||000001||1FST2M6||06-10-2000||09:50 PM||||sounds like you need stickier tires, and a nitrous kit!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||dodger||06-10-2000||11:35 PM||||Definately...I realized my tread was low enough to lose grip...I had enough power, but it was too close...||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||06-11-2000||12:07 AM||||unless I'm strapped for cash I replace tires below about 1/2 their original tread just to prevent stupid stuff like this.<P>It's hard tho, once a Fiero gets loose in back you better know what you are doing. Glad you got lucky and saved it.<P>I hit some spilled soot recently,,, was like hiting a patch of ice. good thing it was a small patch. (Spilled from an overloaded truck comming from the oil refinery.)||||reg||1
Z||000004||batboy||06-11-2000||12:46 AM||||Please don't pull out in front of anymore big trucks...whew! Ogre's right, when a Fiero breaks loose, it will swap ends in a hurry. Did you have to change your shorts?||||reg||1
